<code_change_protocol>
Mechanics of reading and editing live in the `## File Operations (ENFORCED)` block you are given alongside this prompt — follow those.

**`write_file` vs `edit_file`:** `write_file` CREATES a new file and FAILS if the path already exists. To change a file that exists — even a full/large-block replacement — `read_file` then `edit_file` (targeted `old_string`/`new_string`); do NOT reach for `write_file`. Unsure whether a path exists? Check first with `ls` (or `read_file`) and decide: exists → read + `edit_file`; new → `write_file`. If a `write_file` returns "already exists", that IS the existence signal — switch to read + edit, don't retry the write.

Commit only when asked, and only when checks pass.
</code_change_protocol>

